  <i><b><h1>ABOUT US.</h1></b></i>
  <p> To teach the Godly generation to the world. </p>
  <h3>PURPOSE.</h3>
<p>  To preach and teach the lost the word of God to be served in the blood of Jesus.</p>
  <h3>HISTORY.</h3>
<p>Church Youth Gathering Uganda , it started in the year of 2025 /11/10th by Bisoboka Samuel Kezaala by his age of 20 years old. 

He is born in the year of 2005 / 7 / 7 in the village of Kawempe tula and he is the son of Pr Kezaala Stanley and Nakasi Betty. 

He believed Jesus Christ as is personal savior in the year of 2019 at Hope of city deliverance church mission. </p>
  
  <h3>ACTIVITIES.</h3>

<b><h5>  Worship & Spiritual Growth.</h5></b>

<p> Services – Regular worship with sermons, music, and prayer. <br>

Bible Study Groups – Weekly gatherings to study scripture and discuss life applications.<br>

Prayer Meetings / Vigils – Focused times of corporate or personal prayer.<br>

Communion Services – Celebrations of the Lord’s Supper.<br>

Baptism Ceremonies – Welcoming new believers.<br>

Fasting and Spiritual Retreats – Times set apart for reflection and renewal.<br>
<br></p>

  <b><h5>Fellowship & Community.</h5></b>
<p>Church Picnics / Family Days – Fun events that strengthen relationships.<br>

Men’s / Women’s Fellowship – Groups for gender-specific encouragement and mentoring.<br>

Youth Ministry Nights – Games, music, and talks for teens.<br>

Children’s Sunday School – Bible lessons and activities for kids.<br>

Couples’ Fellowship – Marriage enrichment events or discussions.<br>

Small Groups / Cell Meetings – Home-based gatherings for deeper connection.<br>
  <br></p>
 
<b><h5>Music & Creative Arts.</h5></b>
  <br>
<p>
Choir Practice – Preparing for Sunday worship or concerts.
<br>
Drama – Skits or plays with biblical messages.<br>

Dance Ministry / Mime – Worship through movement.<br>

Music Workshops – Training for singers and instrumentalists.
<br>
</p>
<b><h5>Service & Outreach.</h5></b>
<p>
Evangelism / Street Ministry – Sharing the gospel in communities.
<br>
Charity Drives – Food, clothing, or blood donations.
<br>
Hospital / Prison Visits – Ministering to those in need.
<br>
Community Clean-Up Days – Serving the neighborhood.
<br>
Mission Trips – Local or international outreach.
  <br></p>
<b><h5>Education & Development.</h5></b>
<p>Leadership Training – Developing ministry or team leaders.
<br>
Workshops & Seminars – Topics like financial stewardship, parenting, or career growth.
<br>
Discipleship Programs – Courses for spiritual maturity.
<br>
Book Clubs / Reading Groups – Christian literature discussions.
<br></p>
<b><h5> Special Events.</h5></b>
<p>Anniversaries / Founders’ Day
<br>
Easter & Christmas Programs
<br>
Harvest Thanksgiving Services
<br>
Youth / Choir Concerts
  </p>
